Privacy Policy – Werewolf Hero (Web)
Last updated: October 17, 2026

Zimo Games ("we", "us", or "our") operates the web version of the game Werewolf Hero (the "Game"), which is published on CrazyGames (crazygames.com) and its partner websites.

This Privacy Policy explains what information is collected when you play the Game in your web browser, how it is used, and which third parties are involved. The mobile version of the Game is covered by a separate privacy policy.

1. Information We Collect
The Game does not ask you to create an account, and we do not ask for your name, email address, or other contact details inside the Game.

When you play, the following information may be collected automatically:

Gameplay information, such as levels reached, progression, session start and length, and in-game events (for example enemies defeated or player deaths).
Technical information, such as browser type and version, operating system, device type, screen size, and language.
Approximate location (country), which may be inferred from your IP address.
A random identifier stored in your browser, used to recognize returning sessions for analytics. It does not identify you personally.
Diagnostic information, such as errors and performance data.
Information you provide if you contact us for support.
We do not collect advertising identifiers in the web version, and we do not intentionally collect sensitive personal information.

2. How We Use Information
We use this information to:

Provide and operate the Game.
Save your game progress.
Understand how players use the Game and improve gameplay, difficulty, and content.
Find and fix technical problems.
Show advertisements, where the Game displays them.
Prevent abuse and comply with legal obligations.
3. Game Progress and Browser Storage
Your game progress and settings are saved through the CrazyGames platform:

If you are not logged in on CrazyGames, your progress is stored in your browser's local storage on your device. Clearing your browser data deletes it.
If you are logged in on CrazyGames, your progress is stored with your CrazyGames account so it is available on other devices.
The Game and the services below may also use browser storage and similar technologies (such as cookies or local storage) to keep your settings and to measure usage.

4. Third-Party Services
The Game uses the following third-party services, which process information according to their own privacy policies:

CrazyGames
CrazyGames hosts the Game, provides player accounts, stores game progress, and delivers advertisements in the Game. CrazyGames may collect information about your use of its website and the games on it, as described in its privacy policy: https://www.crazygames.com/privacy-policy

GameAnalytics
We use GameAnalytics to understand how the Game is played and to improve it. GameAnalytics may collect gameplay events, technical information about your browser and device, and an approximate location derived from your IP address. https://gameanalytics.com/privacy/

We may add or remove third-party services as the Game develops. If we do, we will update this Privacy Policy.

5. Advertising
The Game may show advertisements, including optional rewarded ads (for example, watching an ad to receive an in-game reward). Advertisements are provided through CrazyGames. Any choices about personalized advertising and cookie consent are managed by CrazyGames on its website.

6. Children's Privacy
The Game is not designed to knowingly collect personal information from children in violation of applicable laws. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the Game in a way that violates applicable law, please contact us and we will take appropriate action.

7. Data Retention
We keep information only as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy, including operating and improving the Game, maintaining security, and complying with legal obligations. Retention periods may vary depending on the type of information and the service involved.

8. Data Security
We take reasonable measures to protect information processed through the Game. However, no method of transmission or electronic storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

9. Your Privacy Rights
Depending on where you live, you may have rights regarding your personal information, such as the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict the processing of your information. You can delete progress stored on your device at any time by clearing your browser data. To make any other privacy-related request, please contact us.

10. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will change the "Last updated" date at the top of this page.

